{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CKrptGNdxknAMaq8DmUvoM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I can see the existing structure. Now let me write the category overview for 02-rag-systems.md. I need to follow the template structure and include all required sections:\n\n1. Interview signals (4-6 trigger phrases)\n2. Mental model (1 paragraph)\n3. Sub-topics (2-4 named sub-areas)\n4. Decision framework (decision tree)\n5. Common mistakes (table)\n6. Question checklist (table with all 34 questions)\n7. One-page summary (3-5 bullets)\n\nThe 34 questions for RAG Systems from the question bank are:\n\nArchitecture & design (11):\n- Design a RAG system for a customer support chatbot and how to evaluate it\n- Design an LLM-powered enterprise search system\n- Design a GenAI document-processing pipeline for unstructured data like emails, PDFs, and images\n- Use GPT-4 to generate accurate answers from proprietary documents\n- Design a generative QA assistant for a company's knowledge base\n- Handle context when splitting large PDF reports into chunks\n- Efficiently generate and store embeddings for products and queries\n- Handle hallucination when the context doesn't contain relevant information\n- Discuss RAG projects I've worked on and design a Q&A system over internal documentation\n- Ensure quality of data that the LLM interacts with\n- Compare sparse versus dense retrieval and when to use each approach\n- Debug common RAG failure points\n- Protect sensitive and confidential data in a RAG pipeline\n- Evaluate different vector databases and their trade-offs\n- Handle document-wide context when chunking, like financial reports with metadata about units\n- Understand hybrid search combining vector and BM25 retrieval\n- Understand re-ranking with cross-encoders versus bi-encoders\n- Scale RAG systems to handle millions of articles with sharding, caching, and retrieval optimization\n- Address cases where RAG returns relevant documents but users still aren't satisfied — the difference between search engines and answer engines\n- Evaluate RAG pipelines using metrics like NDCG, MRR, precision@k, and recall\n- Handle citations and source attribution\n- Understand how ANN search works with HNSW indexing\n- Recognize where embeddings fail, like with negation, temporal reasoning, or precision requirements\n- Use semantic caching to reduce cost and latency\n- Handle multi-turn conversation context in RAG\n- Navigate key tradeoffs between latency and accuracy, chunk size and context window, and cost versus quality\n- Optimize RAG latency in production\n- Identify common failure modes: bad chunking strategies, vocabulary mismatch between queries and documents, lost-in-the-middle effects from context pollution, and hallucinations when retrieved context is irrelevant or missing\n- Account for stale indexes and embedding drift over time\n- Recognize when weak evaluation metrics hide underlying retrieval failures\n\nNow I'm putting together a comprehensive overview of these categories.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":53379,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":283,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa9f5373-3237-46e4-ac93-22e97ebb4ec1","uuid":"daedfc44-1f29-4dc9-bfe2-332798a628e0"}
